e="1" as="geometry"></mxGeometry></mxCell><mxCell id="rel-27" value="" style="fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=13;fontStyle=1;labelBackgroundColor=#ffffff;edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;exitX=0.5;exitY=0;entryX=0.5;entryY=1;html=1;rounded=0;strokeColor=#555555;startArrow=ERmany;endArrow=ERmandOne;startFill=0;endFill=0;startSize=12;endSize=12;" edge="1" parent="1" source="t_INGREDIENT_FUNCTION" target="t_INGREDIENT"><mxGeometry x="0.0" y="0.0" relative="1" as="geometry"></mxGeometry></mxCell><mxCell id="rel-28" value="" style="fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=13;fontStyle=1;labelBackgroundColor=#ffffff;edgeStyle=entityRelationEdgeStyle;html=1;rounded=0;strokeColor=#555555;startArrow=ERmany;endArrow=ERmandOne;startFill=0;endFill=0;startSize=12;endSize=12;" edge="1" parent="1" source="t_INGREDIENT_FLAG" target="t_INGREDIENT"><mxGeometry x="0.0" y="0.0" relative="1" as="geometry"></mxGeometry></mxCell><mxCell id="rnote" value="&lt;b&gt;Mapping rules applied&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;1. Each strong entity becomes a table; its key becomes the primary key.&lt;br&gt;2. Composite attributes (full_name, skin_profile) are flattened into simple columns.&lt;br&gt;3. Derived attributes (age_range, total_duration, safety_score, overall_confidence, rank) are computed, not stored.&lt;br&gt;4. 1:N relationships: foreign key on the N side (e.g. SKIN_ANALYSIS.user_id).&lt;br&gt;5. M:N relationships become junction tables that carry the relationship attributes (ZONE_ASSESSMENT, PREDICTION, PRODUCT_USE, PRODUCT_INGREDIENT); ANSWER holds one row per selected option (multivalued relationship attribute), so a skipped question has no row.&lt;br&gt;6. Multivalued attributes become their own tables (QUESTION_OPTION, INGREDIENT_FUNCTION, INGREDIENT_FLAG).&lt;br&gt;7. Weak entity ROUTINE_STEP: primary key = owner key routine_id + partial key step_no.&lt;br&gt;8. Specialization of PHOTO (disjoint, total): one table per class; each subclass reuses the superclass key (photo_id is both PK and FK) and photo_kind records the subclass.&lt;br&gt;9. 1:1 DOCUMENTS: unique foreign key PROGRESS_PHOTO.log_id.&lt;br&gt;10. Optional 1:N BASED_ON: own table ROUTINE_SOURCE (no NULL, no dependency analysis_id → user_id inside ROUTINE).&lt;br&gt;All 26 tables are in Boyce-Codd normal form (BCNF)." style="text;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;whiteSpace=wrap;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=13;fontSize=12;fillColor=#f5f5f5;strokeColor=#999999;spacing=10;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="1840" y="970" width="1120" height="260" as="geometry"/></mxCell></root></mxGraphModel></diagram><diagram id="map" name="EER to relational"><mxGraphModel dx="1600" dy="1000" grid="1" gridSize="10" guides="1" tooltips="1" connect="1" arrows="1" fold="1" page="1" pageScale="1" pageWidth="4200" pageHeight="2800" math="0" shadow="0"><root><mxCell id="0"/><mxCell id="1" parent="0"/><mxCell id="mtitle" value="&lt;b&gt;From the EER model (top) to the relational schema (bottom)&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;font style='font-size:14px'&gt;Every EER element that becomes a table carries a coloured badge &lt;b&gt;Tn&lt;/b&gt;; the same badge marks the table it produced. A relationship that becomes a foreign key carries a dashed badge &lt;b&gt;FK→Tn&lt;/b&gt; pointing to the table that holds the key. The mapping table (bottom right) gives the rule used for each element. Colours: purple account and security, blue skin analysis, red photos, green products, routines and log.&lt;/font&gt;" style="text;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;whiteSpace=wrap;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=13;fontSize=26;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="200" y="15" width="3900" height="110" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="title" value="&lt;b&gt;AI-Assisted Skincare Companion App: Enhanced Entity-Relationship (EER) model&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;font style='font-size:13px'&gt;Chen notation. Cardinality ratios 1, N, M; a double line marks total participation.&lt;/font&gt;" style="text;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=13;fontSize=22;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="570" y="185" width="1500" height="70" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="USER" value="USER" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#dae8fc;strokeColor=#6c8ebf;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=13;fontStyle=1;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="1830" y="692" width="180" height="56" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="CONSENT" value="CONSENT" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#dae8fc;strokeColor=#6c8ebf;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=13;fontStyle=1;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="710" y="432" width="180" height="56" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="TOKEN_FAMILY" value="TOKEN_FAMILY" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#dae8fc;strokeColor=#6c8ebf;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=13;fontStyle=1;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="710" y="692" width="180" height="56" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="REFRESH_TOKEN" value="REFRESH_TOKEN" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#dae8fc;strokeColor=#6c8ebf;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=13;fontStyle=1;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="160" y="692" width="180" height="56" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="REMINDER" value="REMINDER" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#dae8fc;strokeColor=#6c8ebf;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=13;fontStyle=1;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="710" y="952" width="180" height="56" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="SKIN_ANALYSIS" value="SKIN_ANALYSIS" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#dae8fc;strokeColor=#6c8ebf;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=13;fontStyle=1;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="1230" y="1382" width="180" height="56" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="QUESTION" value="QUESTION" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#dae8fc;strokeColor=#6c8ebf;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=13;fontStyle=1;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="530" y="1282" width="180" height="56" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="FACE_